Build a complete production-ready website for a small Canadian
independent publishing imprint called Anna’s Dad Press, using the
primary domain annasdadpress.com. The owner also controls
annasdadpress.ca, which should eventually redirect to the .com.

Brand story

Anna’s Dad Press grew out of the publisher’s daughter Anna’s
successful Learn Math With Anna self-publishing project. Watching
Anna develop and sell educational books is what inspired her dad
to begin publishing his own educational and puzzle books.

The name should feel intentional, warm and memorable—not jokey or
amateurish. The visual identity should communicate:

intelligent approachable carefully designed educational adult-friendly
independent rather than corporate

Avoid the visual language of a children’s publisher, generic “AI
startup,” or bargain puzzle-book mill.

Initial publishing program

The first major catalog is The Sudoku Learner’s Library, an umbrella
collection of Sudoku instruction and practice books.

Initial/forthcoming books:

The Sudoku Learner’s Guide Subtitle: A Step-by-Step Handbook of
Rules, Techniques, and Practice Grids This is the flagship book: a
full-color, approximately 250-page course that takes a complete
beginner through advanced Sudoku techniques including Full Houses,
Naked and Hidden Singles, Naked and Hidden Pairs, Pointing Pairs,
Y-Wing, X-Wing, Swordfish, Naked Triples, Simple Colors, XY-Chains,
Unique Rectangles and 3D Medusa.  Practice: X-Wing Sudoku A
deliberate-practice workbook that teaches readers to recognize
X-Wing patterns progressively rather than merely supplying random
puzzles.  Start Here: Hard Sudoku with Hints Hard Sudoku in which
hints tell the solver where to look next without simply revealing
the answer.  Candidates Done: Hard Sudoku Hard Sudoku with
candidate/pencil marks already supplied so the reader can skip setup
and start solving the interesting logic.  Mastery: Hard Sudoku A
conventional but carefully graded independent-solving book.

The four future product families are visually and conceptually:

PRACTICE — deliberate training in one specific technique START HERE
— guided full-puzzle solving CANDIDATES DONE — candidate notes
supplied MASTERY — independent puzzle solving

Initially they all belong under the broader Sudoku Learner’s Library
umbrella. The site architecture should allow each family to grow
into its own collection later.

Website goals

The site is primarily a publisher/catalog website, not an ecommerce
store. Purchases will initially go to Amazon.

Its goals are:

establish Anna’s Dad Press as a credible publishing imprint; explain
the origin/story behind the unusual name; showcase the Sudoku
Learner’s Library; help readers determine which book is right for
them; provide stable URLs that can be printed in books and QR codes;
support future books outside Sudoku without requiring a redesign;
rank organically for book titles, series names, and relevant
educational/puzzle searches.  Required pages Home

