Visual system

Create one coherent publishing identity plus distinct visual languages
for the Sudoku families.

The family names should be very prominent:

PRACTICE START HERE CANDIDATES DONE MASTERY

They should share:

typography hierarchy spacing/grid family-label position publisher
identity book-card design

but each should have its own recognizable accent treatment/iconography.

Avoid overly playful exclamation marks in the web identity. The
formal title style is colon-based, e.g. Practice: X-Wing Sudoku.

The site should visually harmonize with sophisticated Sudoku covers:
strong typography, crisp geometric grid motifs, restrained use of
color, generous white space.

Do not use generic stock photographs of people doing puzzles.

See sample_covers/*.png for existing art inspiration.

Technical implementation

Prefer a lightweight static-first architecture built out of pure HTML
or Svelte. Choose the simplest option that produces an excellent result.

Requirements:

excellent desktop and mobile layouts very fast page loads accessible
semantic HTML keyboard navigation WCAG-conscious contrast responsive
images no unnecessary client-side JavaScript data-driven book catalog
easy addition of new books without redesigning pages clean reusable
components favicon and simple typographic/logo treatment no paid
dependencies unless clearly justified SEO

Implement:

unique title/meta description for every page canonical URLs Open
Graph/social metadata sitemap.xml robots.txt Organization/Publisher
schema where appropriate Book structured data on individual book
pages sensible heading hierarchy

Do not keyword-stuff.

Domain/deployment

Use gh to create a github repository, that's public; use cloudflare API keys
to demonstrate control of the domains, making .ca redirect to .com and .com
serve the github pages site.

Deliverables

Produce:

complete deployed site; polished responsive site; README
with local-development and deployment instructions; catalog data
model with the five initial books; placeholders clearly identified
for final cover artwork, ISBNs, ASINs and Amazon URLs; stable /next
page; SEO metadata and structured data; no fake testimonials, reviews, 
awards, bestseller claims or invented business facts.

Before finishing, run the build, test all internal links, inspect
the mobile layout, and finally deploy to gh pages.
